## Report
Rubric used (see rubric field). Dynamic attempts first: `cargo test -p storage delete_bucket_clears_completed_multipart_upload_records -- --nocapture` failed to build due to missing libisal in ec-sys build script (build error shown in artifacts/build_fail.log). Valgrind is not installed (`valgrind --version` -> command not found). gdb is not installed; lldb is present but no binary could be built to debug due to the libisal build failure. Code review: `PgStore::complete_multipart_commit` records a tombstone for every completed upload by inserting into `completed_multipart_uploads` (crates/storage/src/pg_store.rs:5302-5325). The abort path, when the upload is already completed, returns success after fetching the completed record and does not delete it (crates/server-core/src/coordinator.rs:13672-13690). The only delete path for completed multipart records is in bucket deletion (crates/storage/src/pg_store.rs:1623-1645); a repo-wide search shows no other deletes. The table schema has no TTL/expiry mechanism (crates/storage/src/schema.rs:103-118). This means a client with multipart upload permissions can repeatedly complete uploads with unique IDs, leaving persistent tombstones and causing unbounded metadata DB growth until bucket deletion.

